---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
// Assuming your renamed image is in src/assets/
import journalHero from '../assets/luxury-wedding-invitations-nairobi.jpg';
---

<Layout title="The Journal | Ateliér Bespoke">
  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto py-24 px-6">
    <header class="mb-16 border-b border-gray-100 pb-12">
      <h1 class="text-5xl font-serif italic mb-4">The Journal</h1>
      <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.4em] text-gray-400">Insights into the Craft</p>
    </header>

    <article class="mb-24">
      <Image 
        src={journalHero} 
        alt="Bespoke luxury wedding invitations in Nairobi featuring mauve cardstock and wax seals" 
        class="w-full h-auto mb-8 grayscale hover:grayscale-0 transition-all duration-700 shadow-sm"
      />
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-serif mb-6 italic text-gray-800">The Power of Tangible Identity in a Digital World</h2>
      <div class="prose prose-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed space-y-4">
        <p>
          In the heart of Nairobi, a new standard of luxury is emerging. It isn't found in a logo on a screen, but in the weight of a <strong>bespoke invitation suite</strong> or the distinct snap of a <strong>custom wax seal</strong>.
        </p>
        <p>
          For the 2026 season, Kenyan brands and milestones are leaning into <em>Inevitable Design</em>—branding that feels as though it has always existed. From Westlands boardrooms to Karen garden weddings, the tactile touchpoint remains the ultimate mark of authority.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
